       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The reason you gave, getting everything settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for a dose five times the 10 mg maximum. Entering it could seriously harm the patient. Nothing in the chart you described, including normal kidney and liver function, supports it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a standard dose:** I can enter amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily right now. You can titrate later, since the full effect takes about 1\u20132 weeks.\n- **Help with timing:** If the goal is better blood pressure control before evening rounds, amlodipine works slowly and isn't the right tool for that. Your team or pharmacy may suggest a faster-acting option.\n- **Get a second review:** If you think this patient needs an unusual dose, I'd suggest talking to pharmacy or your attending first. I can enter the order with a note once that's documented.\n\nTell me which of these you want, and I'll enter the order."
      }
